1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,500
This is a Polish public tender notice.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Somewhere in here are the deadline, the bid security and the list of documents. Miss one line and your offer is rejected.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Tender Lens opens next to the notice.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Before any AI runs, a local parser already found the deadline, the bid security and the award criteria.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Now the AI part. The GDPR clauses and platform manuals were removed locally,

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:50,000
the rest fits Gemini Nano's window, so Firebase AI Logic runs it right here in Chrome, on my computer.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:02,000
I get a summary in English, the conditions, the criteria and the things a small company could miss, like references with a minimum value.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Same request in the cloud: same JSON schema, different engine.

9
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Each answer is labelled, so you always know where your data went.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Requests for quotation from EU projects work too.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
For the long specification, text is extracted on my computer first.

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Ninety-six pages is too much for the on-device model, so the original PDF goes to Gemini in the cloud.

13
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:01,000
If I don't want anything to leave my computer, on-device only mode

14
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:12,000
splits a longer document into several Gemini Nano passes and merges the results.

15
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The checklist is what I actually work from.

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Watched tenders sync through Cloud Firestore with an anonymous account, and the deadline goes to my calendar with reminders three days and one day before.

17
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Under the hood: Firebase AI Logic hybrid inference, App Check, Authentication, Firestore and Remote Config.

18
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Tender Lens. Read the notice, not the boilerplate.
